nge of position of a mechanical component with time. Within Sensors and Transducers, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of velocity within Mechatronics, particularly where the Sensors and Transducers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of velocity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'velocity; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of velocity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Mechatronics', 'Active'), ('KCR_000508', 'force', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mechatronics', 'Technical Concept', 'An interaction that produces acceleration or deformation and is measured or controlled in mechatronic systems.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of force within Mechatronics, particularly where the Sensors and Transducers module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of force, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'An interaction that produces acceleration or deformation and is measured or controlled in mechatronic systems. Within Sensors and Transducers, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of force within Mechatronics, particularly where the Sensors and Transducers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of force, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'force; Core considerations includ