 it.', 'Actuators that convert compressed air or pressurised fluid into controlled mechanical motion. Within Actuators and Drives, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of pneumatic and hydraulic actuators within Mechatronics, particularly where the Actuators and Drives module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of pneumatic and hydraulic actuators, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'pneumatic and hydraulic actuators; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of pneumatic and hydraulic actuators, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Mechatronics', 'Active'), ('KCR_000515', 'microcontrollers', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mechatronics', 'Technical Concept', 'Integrated programmable devices that combine a processor, memory, and peripheral interfaces for dedicated control and embedded-system tasks.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of microcontrollers within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of microcontrollers, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Integrated programmable devices that combine a processor, memory, and peripheral interfaces for dedicated control and embedded-system tasks. Within Embedded Controllers, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of microcontrollers within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of microcontrollers, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'microcontrollers; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of microcontrollers, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Mechatronics', 'Active'), ('KCR_000516', 'Input/Output (I/O)', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mechatronics', 'Technical Concept', 'Input/output interfaces through which a controller exchanges signals with sensors, actuators, and other devices.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of I/O within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of I/O, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Input/output interfaces through which a controller exchanges signals with sensors, actuators, and other devices. Within Embedded Controllers, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of I/O within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of I/O, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'I/O; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of I/O, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Mechatronics', 'Active'), ('KCR_000517', 'timers', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mechatronics', 'Technical Concept', 'Controller hardware or software functions that generate timing events, delays, or periodic operations.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of timers within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of timers, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Controller hardware or software functions that generate timing events, delays, or periodic operations. Within Embedded Controllers, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of timers within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of timers, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'timers; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of timers, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Mechatronics', 'Active'), ('KCR_000518', 'interrupts', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mechatronics', 'Technical Concept', 'Signals that temporarily divert processor execution to handle an event requiring timely service.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of interrupts within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of interrupts, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Signals that temporarily divert processor execution to handle an event requiring timely service. Within Embedded Controllers, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of interrupts within Mechatronics, particularly where the Embedded Controllers module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of interrupts, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'interrupts; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of interrupts, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Mechatronics', 'Active'), ('KCR_000519', 'Analog-to-Digital / Digital-to-Analog Conversion (ADC/DAC)', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Mechatronics; Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation', 'Technical Concept', 'Analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog conversion processes used to interface continuous-valued signals with digital systems.', 'Concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'Defining mechanism/properties; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria for ADC/DAC.', 'Analog-to-digital and digital-to-analog conversion processes used to interface continuous-valued signals with digital systems. Within Embedded Controllers; Signal Conditioning and Data Acquisition, the concept covers Concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules. Key technical considerations are Defining mechanism/properties; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria for ADC/DAC.', 'ADC/DAC; Defining mechanism/properties; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria